C Synthetic example orbit for teaching purposes (not a real star).
C Physically self-consistent: the astrometric mass (from a, P, parallax)
C and spectroscopic mass (from K1, K2) agree, as they should for a real binary.
C Try running a fit as-is, then experiment: uncheck some Fit boxes,
C or nudge a starting value and re-run to see how the fit responds.
